//RS /// Append one workflow record and advance the in-memory history by replaying
//RS /// it.  The record is applied to the replayed durable log first, so a payload
//RS /// the reader would reject never reaches the store, and a history that has
//RS /// drifted from the store is reported instead of extended.  The extra read
//RS /// costs one more pass over a store the append already re-reads.
//RS ///
//RS /// The workflow file lock orders writers across processes. The state append
//RS /// below also takes the shared process lock before it publishes the record.
